<title>PAKISTAN: Pakistani cotton market close on strike.</title>
<headline>Pakistani cotton market close on strike.</headline>
<dateline>KARACHI, Pakistan 1996-10-26</dateline>
<text>
<p>The Pakistani cotton market remained shut on Saturday due to a strike called by opposition parties and a business group to protest against new taxes and a devaluation of the rupee, dealers said.</p>
<p>Thursday's official spot rates issued by the Karachi Cotton Association in rupees per maund were:  Thurs	 Wed</p>
<p>    NIAB-78				    2,432.50    2,432.50</p>
<p>    K-68					 2,460.00    2,460.00</p>
<p>    MNH-93				     2,470.00    2,415.00</p>
<p>($1 = 40.22 Pakistani rupees)</p>
<p>-- Amir Zia 9221-5685192</p>
</text>
